+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running Tarantool
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Tarantool is started from an instance script passed on the command
line.  An example script is installed as:

	${TRUEPREFIX}/share/examples/tarantool/init.lua

Copy it into place and adjust it to your needs:

	# mkdir -p ${SYSCONFDIR}/tarantool
	# cp ${TRUEPREFIX}/share/examples/tarantool/init.lua \
		${SYSCONFDIR}/tarantool/init.lua

The rc.d(8) script is installed and enabled with:

	# rcctl enable tarantool
	# rcctl start tarantool

Tarantool runs as the _tarantool user.  Its data, log and pid files
live in ${LOCALSTATEDIR}/db/tarantool, /var/log/tarantool and
/var/run/tarantool respectively.

The interactive console and the tarantool(1) command line can be used
to manage an instance:

	$ tarantool
	localhost> box.cfg{listen = 3301}
